---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About Lumma Creative Studio" description="Learn about Lumma Creative Studio, its educational direction, and the relationship between Lumma and Aya.">
  <section class="page-hero about-hero">
    <div class="container about-hero-grid">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">About Lumma</span>
        <h1 class="display">Building thoughtful learning experiences for Muslim families.</h1>
        <p class="lead">Lumma Creative Studio brings together education, storytelling, language, publishing, technology, and creative development to create useful learning experiences.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="about-principle-card">
        <span class="tag">Our direction</span>
        <strong>Learning should feel connected to real family life.</strong>
        <p>We develop experiences that are practical, age-appropriate, meaningful, and designed to be revisited.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container about-grid">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">What Lumma does</span>
        <h2 class="title">A studio working across education and creative technology.</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="lead">Our work can take different forms: content channels, learning platforms, books, educational resources, and digital experiences. The format changes according to the learning need, while the underlying direction stays consistent.</p>
        <p>We care about clarity, usefulness, cultural and religious sensitivity, strong storytelling, and interfaces that are easy for families to use.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-soft">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Lumma & Aya</span>
      <h2 class="title">Lumma builds. Aya connects.</h2>
      <div class="about-relationship-grid">
        <article class="about-role-card">
          <span class="role-index">01</span>
          <h3>Lumma Creative Studio</h3>
          <p>The organisation and creative studio responsible for developing educational content, products, platforms, and digital experiences.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="about-role-card about-role-accent">
          <span class="role-index">02</span>
          <h3>Aya</h3>
          <p>The central character and educational universe through which related stories, learning experiences, platforms, and products can connect.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container about-values-grid">
      <div><span class="eyebrow">How we think</span><h2 class="title">Useful first. Thoughtful throughout.</h2></div>
      <div class="about-values-list">
        <div><strong>Purposeful learning</strong><p>Each experience should have a clear educational reason to exist.</p></div>
        <div><strong>Family context</strong><p>Learning is stronger when it can connect with conversations, routines, and shared use.</p></div>
        <div><strong>Age-appropriate design</strong><p>Language, presentation, pacing, and interaction should respect the learner's stage.</p></div>
        <div><strong>Responsible technology</strong><p>Digital tools should serve the learning experience rather than become the experience itself.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
